the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the code of the violation is *a text*.
    the date of the violation is *a date*.
    the type of the violation is *a text*.
    the speed limit of the violation is *a number*.
    the actual speed of the violation is *a number*.
    the name of the driver is *a text*.
    the age of the driver is *a number*.
    the state of the driver is *a text*.
    the city of the driver is *a text*.
    the points of the driver is *a number*.
    the amount of the fine is *a number*.
    the points of the fine is *a number*.
    the should the driver be suspended is *a text*.
    the total points of the should the driver be suspended is *a value*.

the knowledge base traffic_violation includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/Traffic Violation.dmn".

rule fine_1 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 1:
the amount of the fine is 500 if
    the type of the violation is "speed"
    and the actual speed of the violation - the speed limit of the violation >= 10
    and the actual speed of the violation - the speed limit of the violation < 30.

rule fine_2 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 1:
the points of the fine is 3 if
    the type of the violation is "speed"
    and the actual speed of the violation - the speed limit of the violation >= 10
    and the actual speed of the violation - the speed limit of the violation < 30.

rule fine_3 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 2:
the amount of the fine is 1000 if
    the type of the violation is "speed"
    and the actual speed of the violation - the speed limit of the violation >= 30.

rule fine_4 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 2:
the points of the fine is 7 if
    the type of the violation is "speed"
    and the actual speed of the violation - the speed limit of the violation >= 30.

rule fine_5 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 3:
the amount of the fine is 100 if
    the type of the violation is "parking".

rule fine_6 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 3:
the points of the fine is 1 if
    the type of the violation is "parking".

rule fine_7 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 4:
the amount of the fine is 1000 if
    the type of the violation is "driving under the influence".

rule fine_8 with provenance the model at decision Fine rule 4:
the points of the fine is 5 if
    the type of the violation is "driving under the influence".

rule should_the_driver_be_suspended_1 with provenance the model at decision Should the driver be suspended?:
the total points of the should the driver be suspended is a value V if
    V = the points of the driver + the points of the fine.

rule should_the_driver_be_suspended_2 with provenance the model at decision Should the driver be suspended?:
the should the driver be suspended is "Yes" if
    the total points of the should the driver be suspended >= 20.

rule should_the_driver_be_suspended_3 with provenance the model at decision Should the driver be suspended?:
the should the driver be suspended is "No" if
    it is not the case that
        the total points of the should the driver be suspended is a value V
        and V >= 20.

